course: dictionary
lesson: 14952
title: Relate: connecting things and people
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Relate is a verb, and it is about connection. When two things relate, there is a link between them. In maths, you might ask, «How does the length relate to the width?» That means: how are they connected?
explain: When you relate to someone, you understand how they feel because you have felt the same. If your friend says, «I can relate» after you tell her about a lost tooth, she means she felt the same too.
explain: Relate can also mean to tell a story, usually in a formal way. «The old sailor began to relate his adventures at sea.» Here he is telling his story.
explain: Related people belong to the same family. Your cousin is related to you, even if you have never met before. Use the context to pick the right meaning: look at what is around the word and ask yourself which meaning fits.
fact: Relate is a verb: relate, relates, related, relating.
fact: «Relate to» means to be connected with something, as in «How does this relate to the topic?»
fact: «I can relate» means «I feel the same as you.»
fact: Related people belong to the same family, and related words are words that share a meaning or a root.
fact: Formal writing may use relate to mean tell, as in «relate a story».
exercise: When Sam says «I can relate», what does he mean? | He has lost his bag | He is too tired to talk | *He feels the same as you | He is going to the shops
exercise: «Ava and Sam are related: they share a grandad.» What does related mean here? | Have the same shoes | *Belong to the same family | Are good at maths | Are very tall
exercise: «Can you relate the shadow to the time of day?» What is the task? | Paint a shadow | *Connect the shadow with the time | Count the shadows | Hide from the sun
test: «The old sailor began to relate his adventures at sea.» What does relate mean here? | To sleep | *To tell, in a formal way | To forget | To paint
test: «How does the length relate to the width?» What is being asked? | How wide the paper is | *How the two are connected | What colour the shape is | Which side is longer
exam: Which is the best meaning of «related words» in «Find three related words»? | Words that rhyme | Only long words | Words written in red | *Words connected in meaning or form
